        "id": 208268,
        "name": "Rabit",
        "username": "Rabit",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-11-10T21:18:59.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Paul\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/paul/48/5862_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Paul:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p><span class=\"mention\">@JeysieI</span> believe we are going to be able to set it up so that anyone purchasing the physical version can get a free PDF. Stay tuned! <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That is awesome!!! As a GM, having the PDF is so much easier to work with. Pathfinder made me really happy with that, but I always bought the physical books also to support them. Now with 5th Ed D&amp;D, I don't have that, and it's really frustrating.&nbsp;</p>",
